# The configuration errors of msil/test/Programs/c-testsuite (plan 5.12.9;
# M23): a malformed or stale libc-free.txt must stop lit, never turn into
# fewer tests. (1) Inputs/ctest-lists.py unit calls msil_ctest_format's
# TestList and libc_free directly (python -B: no __pycache__ in the source
# tree): a diag entry whose item is not P3-A or P3-B, a diag entry without
# '# <item>', a header count that differs from the entries, a name listed
# twice and a list without '# rule:' are errors, and libc_free picks the .c
# files that the rule matches nowhere. (2) The checks of c-testsuite's
# lit.local.cfg, in nested lits over a copy of the directory
# (Inputs/nested-ctest runs the copy's lit.local.cfg) with a fake cache
# (Inputs/make-fake-corpus.py, then Inputs/ctest-lists.py setup writes the
# tree free1.c, free2.c and calls.c and a matching list): the consistent
# list loads and yields one test per name; a listed test whose .c.expected
# is not empty, a listed name that the tree lacks, a libc-free test of the
# tree that the list lacks, and a name listed twice are each a configuration
# error (lit's exit status 2) that names it. (3) The format's tests executed
# (prog/Inputs/nested-ctest runs the copy's lit.local.cfg below
# prog/lit.local.cfg, so %{msil_prog} and %{msil_prog_fail_<L>} build with
# the stand-ins of prog/Inputs/prog-cc.py, whose compiler accepts only
# c-testsuite's flags there): Inputs/ctest-lists.py setup ... exec lists
# free1, a program that exits 0, and the diag entries diag1, whose compile
# fails with the listed text, and diag2, which builds. At -O0 and -O2,
# free1's MSIL build (and, where the native oracle runs, its native build)
# gets --cflags='-std=gnu17 -w', each compile has those flags, and the runs
# compare with the copy's exit0.expected; diag1 runs 'not' + the build piped
# into FileCheck of the copy's diag.check with "-DDIAG=<text>" and both
# --implicit-check-not texts (LLVM ERROR, PLEASE submit) at each level and
# passes; diag2, whose build succeeds, fails. Under msil_pipeline=lto free1
# passes and both diag entries are UNSUPPORTED (they require
# msil-prog-pipeline=obj).

# (1)
